{
  "$schema": "https://metais.org/schemas/conformance/1/vector.schema.json",
  "id": "sec/input-values",
  "title": "Every reader counts the values it decodes against input-values, which passes at the bound and refuses one value over it",
  "statements": [
    "MTS-SEC-059"
  ],
  "since": "1.0",
  "class": "processor",
  "tags": [],
  "requires": [],
  "notes": "Each form's count, at the bound: j.json {\"a\": [1, 2], \"b\": null} is 5, its root included; y.yaml the same document, 5; an empty YAML document is null, 1; c.csv is its array, each record's object and each field but the unquoted empty one: 1 + 3 + 4 = 8; t.txt 1; m.md with frontmatter its object, title, tags and its two items, and body, 6; without, its object and body, 2; with empty frontmatter, whose mapping is the object, the same 2; collection k is its array and items [1] and {}, 1 + 2 + 1 = 4; --set 1; --set-json {\"a\": [1]} 3; --inputs-json {\"j\": [1, 2]} 4, its root included.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "json-at-the-bound",
      "steps": [
        {
          "op": "validate",
          "args": {
            "package": "package",
            "data": "data/json",
            "limits": {
              "input-values": 5
            }
          },
          "expect": {
            "ok": true
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "json-one-over",
      "steps": [
        {
          "op": "validate",
          "args": {
            "package": "package",
            "data": "data/json",
            "limits": {
              "input-values": 4
            }
          },
          "expect": {
            "ok": false,
            "findings": "expected/json-over.json"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
